@node GUI mechanics
@section GUI mechanics
GUI uses the ncurses library. The method of a FSM separate from FSM of game library.
Scoring records and saving them to a file is implemented in GUI, not in the game library.
The player selects games using the left and right keys. Q is the output. Enter - the game starts. The rest of the keys are designed for gaming.
Pressing the keys is accompanied by a graphic effect in the lower field.
@node Game mechanics
@section Game mechanics
Realised Game mechanics:
@itemize  *
@item Rotation of pieces;
@item Horizontal movement of pieces;
@item Acceleration of the piece's fall (when the button is pressed, the piece moves all the way down);
@item Displaying the next piece;
@item Destruction of filled rows;
@item End of the game when the top of the board is reached;
@item All default types of pieces was included in the game.
@end itemize 
Use these buttons to control the game:
@itemize  *
@item S — for start the game;
@item P — pause;
@item Q — end game and exit to selecting menu;
@item Left arrow — move the piece to the left;
@item Right arrow — move piece to the right;
@item Down arrow — piece falls;
@item Space button — action (piece rotation).
@end itemize 

From time to time, the timer is triggered and the figure goes down one line.

@node Scoring
@section Scoring
Points are awarded when filling in the lines. Points are accumulated as follows:
@itemize  *
@item 1 row is 100 points;
@item 2 rows is 300 points;
@item 3 rows is 700 points;
@item 4 rows is 1500 points.
@end itemize 
Each time a player earns 600 points, the level increases by 1. 
Increasing the level increases the speed at which the pieces move. 
The maximum number of levels is 10.

@node Makefile targets
@chapter Makefile targets
@menu
* Makefile targets::         all, install, uninstall, clear, dvi, dist, test, gcov_report
@end menu
@node all
@section all
The same as "make install".
@node install
@section install
Use "make install" to build the game and place files in directory specified in "EXEC_PREFIX" variable in Makefile.
DVI file will create.
@node uninstall
@section uninstall
Use "make uninstall" to remove directory with game specified in "EXEC_PREFIX" variable in Makefile.
@node clear
@section clear
Delete the auxiliary directory.
@node dvi
@section dvi
Use "make dvi" to create DVI file with this user guide. Use "make dvi_pdf" to create PDF file with this user guide. 
@node dist
@section dist
Use "make dist" to contain distributive files (sources) to archive.
@node test
@section test
For make test with game (only game) library.
@node gcov_report
@section gcov_report
Use "make gcov_report" to prepare test coverage report. Use "make gcov_report_open" to open html report in browser.
